layout "layouts/base.faqir"

block title
  | {{ page.title }}

  link(rel="alternate" type="text/plain" href="/llms.txt" title="llms.txt")
  link(rel="alternate" type="application/json" href="/openapi.json" title="OpenAPI")

block body
  include "partials/site-header.faqir" (current="/for-agents")
  main#main(data-site="marketing" data-gap="12")
    div(data-ui="backdrop" data-variant="grid" data-intensity="subtle")
      div(data-ui="container" data-measure="wide" data-gutter="4")
        section(data-ui="hero" data-variant="center" data-animate aria-labelledby="agents-headline")
          span(data-ui="badge" data-part="eyebrow" data-variant="primary") For agents
          h1(data-part="headline" id="agents-headline") If you are an agent, start here.
          p(data-part="description") Four steps: get a key, read the contract, connect, call. Everything below is plain text you can copy. A person can follow along too.
          div(data-part="actions")
            a(data-ui="button" data-variant="primary" data-size="lg" href="/llms.txt") Read /llms.txt
            a(data-ui="button" data-variant="outline" data-size="lg" href="/openapi.json") Fetch /openapi.json

    div(data-ui="container" data-measure="content" data-gutter="4")
      article(data-ui="prose" aria-labelledby="agents-headline")
        h2#get-a-key 1. Get a key
        p
          | Keys start with
          code fc_live_
          | and belong to one workspace. The secret is shown once; send it as a bearer token on every request.
        ol
          li
            | Sign up at
            a(href="/signup") /signup
            | and a workspace is created with your account.
          li
            | In the dashboard, open
            a(href="/app/keys") API keys
            | and create a key. Name it after the agent that will hold it.
          li Store the secret where the agent reads its environment.
        p Running forecraft yourself? The seed prints a demo key, once:
        div(l-data="{ copied: false }")
          div(data-ui="cluster" data-justify="between")
            span(data-ui="text" data-variant="mono" data-size="xs") shell
            button(data-ui="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm" type="button" @click="navigator.clipboard.writeText($refs.code.textContent); copied = true" l-text="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy'") Copy
          pre(data-lang="bash")
            code(l-ref="code") {{ page.code.seed }}
        p Then put the URL and the key where your tools can read them:
        div(l-data="{ copied: false }")
          div(data-ui="cluster" data-justify="between")
            span(data-ui="text" data-variant="mono" data-size="xs") shell
            button(data-ui="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm" type="button" @click="navigator.clipboard.writeText($refs.code.textContent); copied = true" l-text="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy'") Copy
          pre(data-lang="bash")
            code(l-ref="code") {{ page.code.env }}

        h2#read-the-contract 2. Read the contract
        ul
          li
            a(href="/llms.txt") /llms.txt
            |  — the whole product in one text file, written for you.
          li
            a(href="/openapi.json") /openapi.json
            |  — every endpoint, request and response, as OpenAPI.
          li
            a(href="/docs/for-agents") /docs/for-agents
            |  — the exact curl sequence: create, preview, publish, submit, list, export.
          li
            a(href="/docs/definitions") /docs/definitions
            |  — the form definition: schema, ui, rules, appearance.
          li
            a(href="/docs/mcp") /docs/mcp
            |  — the MCP server: install, tools, resources.
          li
            code GET /api/v1/vocabulary
            |  — the themes, accents and layouts a definition may name.

        h2#connect-over-mcp 3. Connect over MCP
        p
          | Add the server to your host's
          code .mcp.json
          |  (Claude Code reads it from the project root). It speaks stdio and wraps the same REST API.
        div(l-data="{ copied: false }")
          div(data-ui="cluster" data-justify="between")
            span(data-ui="text" data-variant="mono" data-size="xs") .mcp.json
            button(data-ui="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm" type="button" @click="navigator.clipboard.writeText($refs.code.textContent); copied = true" l-text="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy'") Copy
          pre(data-lang="json")
            code(l-ref="code") {{ page.code.mcp }}
        div(role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="MCP tools")
          table
            caption The tools
            thead
              tr
                th(scope="col") Tool
                th(scope="col") What it does
            tbody
              each tool in page.tools
                tr
                  td
                    code {{ tool.name }}
                  td {{ tool.does }}
        p
          | The resource
          code forecraft://form/{id}
          |  returns a form's definition.

        h2#call-the-api 4. Or call the API
        p A first call, to check the key:
        div(l-data="{ copied: false }")
          div(data-ui="cluster" data-justify="between")
            span(data-ui="text" data-variant="mono" data-size="xs") curl
            button(data-ui="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm" type="button" @click="navigator.clipboard.writeText($refs.code.textContent); copied = true" l-text="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy'") Copy
          pre(data-lang="bash")
            code(l-ref="code") {{ page.code.first }}
        p
          | It answers
          code { "items": [] }
          |  for a new workspace. Then create a form:
        div(l-data="{ copied: false }")
          div(data-ui="cluster" data-justify="between")
            span(data-ui="text" data-variant="mono" data-size="xs") curl
            button(data-ui="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm" type="button" @click="navigator.clipboard.writeText($refs.code.textContent); copied = true" l-text="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy'") Copy
          pre(data-lang="bash")
            code(l-ref="code") {{ page.code.create }}
        p
          | Next:
          a(href="/docs/for-agents") the full curl sequence
          | — preview, publish, submit, list and export.

        h2#rules-of-the-road Rules of the road
        ul
          raw
            <li><strong>Errors</strong> are <code>application/problem+json</code> (RFC 9457): <code>type</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>detail</code> and <code>errors[]</code>. Each error has a JSON <code>pointer</code>; a rejected submission also names the <code>field</code> and the <code>rule</code> it broke.</li>
            <li><strong>Rate limit:</strong> 240 requests a minute per key, announced in <code>RateLimit-*</code> headers. A 429 carries <code>Retry-After</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Drafts and versions:</strong> edits change the draft; publish snapshots it. The public URL serves the latest published version.</li>
            <li><strong>Check your work:</strong> preview returns <code>audit.passed</code> and the findings. Publish what passes.</li>
  include "partials/site-footer.faqir"
